{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00292",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.35,
      "end_seconds": 4.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Good morning, how are you doing today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 4.94,
      "end_seconds": 5.64,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Hi."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.59,
      "end_seconds": 10.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "Tell me from the beginning, what's been happening?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.66,
      "end_seconds": 29.55,
      "duration_seconds": 17.89,
      "text": "I've been feeling suddenly very hungry, and I wanted to get it checked. So, I've also been sweating, for about two weeks. Yeah, you know, about sweating, mild, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 31.23,
      "end_seconds": 35.8,
      "duration_seconds": 4.57,
      "text": "What about a pounding heart with it, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 37.7,
      "end_seconds": 46.78,
      "duration_seconds": 9.08,
      "text": "Yes, um, I have. As for pounding heart with it, mostly mild. I'd say on and off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 48.1,
      "end_seconds": 53.79,
      "duration_seconds": 5.69,
      "text": "Have you been feeling suddenly very hungry at any time before this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 57.33,
      "end_seconds": 67.1,
      "duration_seconds": 9.77,
      "text": "Yes, something like this happened about six months ago, and it went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 68.73,
      "end_seconds": 70.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "Any losing consciousness or vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 72.98,
      "end_seconds": 76.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "Oh, no, not any of them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.12,
      "end_seconds": 81.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "Have you noticed weight loss or seizure?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.34,
      "end_seconds": 87.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "No, uh, not any of them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.2,
      "end_seconds": 91.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.28,
      "text": "How are your joints, any aches elsewhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 93.34,
      "end_seconds": 95.3,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "No, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 95.94,
      "end_seconds": 98.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "Anything different when you pass water?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.09,
      "end_seconds": 100.72,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "Nothing there, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.71,
      "end_seconds": 105.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "Anyone in the family with similar problems or other conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.37,
      "end_seconds": 112.02,
      "duration_seconds": 4.65,
      "text": "My mother has migraines. My brother has asthma."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 124.47,
      "end_seconds": 127.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "What about operations, anything like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.55,
      "end_seconds": 133.69,
      "duration_seconds": 5.14,
      "text": "I had my thyroid operated on a long time ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.33,
      "end_seconds": 142.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "Are you on any tablets or medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 143.84,
      "end_seconds": 155.4,
      "duration_seconds": 11.56,
      "text": "Oh, it's ramipril, 5 milligrams, every morning for my blood pressure. Okay, so I take metformin, 500 milligrams, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 156.96,
      "end_seconds": 161.8,
      "duration_seconds": 4.84,
      "text": "Doctor, our chart from the last visit lists it as 1000 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 162.85,
      "end_seconds": 167.86,
      "duration_seconds": 5.01,
      "text": "So, hm, that's different. Is the latest prescription anywhere near you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 169.64,
      "end_seconds": 174.06,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "Not with me. I'll bring it next time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 175.43,
      "end_seconds": 179.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "Tell me about your health in general, any ongoing conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.6,
      "end_seconds": 187.27,
      "duration_seconds": 5.67,
      "text": "I've had high blood pressure for about ten years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 188.06,
      "end_seconds": 188.76,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 189.41,
      "end_seconds": 198.98,
      "duration_seconds": 9.57,
      "text": "I've had diabetes for nearly five years now. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.57,
      "end_seconds": 201.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "Okay, and what else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 203.66,
      "end_seconds": 209.5,
      "duration_seconds": 5.84,
      "text": "Alright, high blood pressure and diabetes, that matches what I have here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.41,
      "end_seconds": 222.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "Now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 224.21,
      "end_seconds": 236.63,
      "duration_seconds": 12.42,
      "text": "Retired. I stopped a few years back. I skip breakfast most days. I live with my family, my husband and two kids."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 237.86,
      "end_seconds": 240.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "Before I prescribe anything, any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 242.18,
      "end_seconds": 245.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "Yes, shellfish. I get vomiting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 247.04,
      "end_seconds": 255.58,
      "duration_seconds": 8.54,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Saturation 98 percent, temp 36.5 degrees, pulse 81. Blood pressure 122 over 72."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.31,
      "end_seconds": 257.6,
      "duration_seconds": 1.29,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 258.76,
      "end_seconds": 262.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "Okay, I need to examine you for this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.52,
      "end_seconds": 265.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "Take your time, no rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.66,
      "end_seconds": 283.83,
      "duration_seconds": 4.17,
      "text": "Pulse is normal and there's no tremor right now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 289.74,
      "end_seconds": 292.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "That's all I need, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 299.48,
      "end_seconds": 308.18,
      "duration_seconds": 8.7,
      "text": "Okay, thinking it through, this looks most like low sugar episodes related to diabetes medication. We shouldn't forget a meal-timing issue."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 308.93,
      "end_seconds": 314.16,
      "duration_seconds": 5.23,
      "text": "I mean, is this something I'll have for good?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 314.99,
      "end_seconds": 352.31,
      "duration_seconds": 37.32,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like low sugar episodes related to diabetes medication, but I'd like to confirm. I think an HbA1c makes sense here, for diabetes control. We should do a blood sugar test for hypoglycaemia. Always keep glucose tablets or a sweet in your bag, and don't skip meals if you've taken your sugar tablet. Cut down on salt and fried food for now, it really does make a difference."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 353.93,
      "end_seconds": 362.97,
      "duration_seconds": 9.04,
      "text": "And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 363.84,
      "end_seconds": 366.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "Right, uh, will do."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 367.48,
      "end_seconds": 373.92,
      "duration_seconds": 6.44,
      "text": "Let's plan a check in two weeks. That's everything from me. Any other questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 374.53,
      "end_seconds": 376.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Thanks so much, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 378.92,
      "end_seconds": 380.68,
      "duration_seconds": 1.76,
      "text": "Mind how you go."
    }
  ]
}